Description: Never let the ratings server hide the application catalogue
 RatingsHelper fetches star ratings from https://odrs.gnome.org at startup, and
 PackageKitSource only emits its category, search and installed lists from the
 RatingsHelper::fetched signal. That request is the store's only network
 dependency: with no route to odrs - offline, behind a captive portal, or on a
 network that answers with an IPv6 address the host cannot reach - the signal
 never arrives and every category stays empty forever. The application
 catalogue itself is local AppStream data and has no reason to wait.
 .
 Give the request a four-second transfer timeout and a four-second fallback
 timer; whichever comes first emits fetched once. When the ratings are
 unavailable the catalogue is shown without them.
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
